<p>Dear Alex,</p>
<p>Thank you for Kestrel's mark-up of clause 12, which we have discussed
with our purchasing and risk colleagues. Our revised draft (v2) is
attached. In short:</p>
<p>1. General cap: we cannot go down to 100%. As a compromise we offer 150%
of the Annual Fees.<br>
2. Data breach: this must remain uncapped. Kestrel's monitoring service
will connect to our plant networks, and under our group policy every
supplier with network access accepts unlimited liability for data breaches.
We are not able to deviate from this.<br>
3. Indirect loss: we accept a mutual exclusion of indirect and
consequential loss. However, costs of production stoppage caused by
defective products are direct loss for us and must remain recoverable
within the cap.</p>
<p>Please let us know whether Kestrel can accept this. We would like to
finalise clause 12 this week.</p>
<p>As requested, we have added your reference {{REF:G02}} to the subject
line.</p>
<p>Best regards</p>
<p>Dr Felix Brandt<br>
Legal Counsel<br>
Acme Automotive GmbH | Legal Department<br>
